================================================================================
CHALLENGE: THE PRIVATE CONTEXT (ThreadLocal)
================================================================================
SCENARIO: You are building a secure backend. Every request thread needs to
know which user is calling it, but you don't want to pass 'String userName'
as a parameter into 20 different methods.

1. CLASS: 'UserSession'
   - Create: 'public static ThreadLocal<String> currentUser = new ThreadLocal<>();'

2. CLASS: 'ServiceRequest' (implements Runnable)
   - FIELDS: 'String name'
   - 'run()' LOGIC:
        * 1. UserSession.currentUser.set(name);
        * 2. Call a method: 'logActivity()';
        * 3. CRITICAL: UserSession.currentUser.remove(); // Essential for clean up!

3. METHOD: 'logActivity()' (Place this in a separate class or as a static helper)
   - LOGIC: Print: Thread.getName() + " is performing action for: " + UserSession.currentUser.get();

4. MAIN:
   - Start 3 threads with names: "Varun", "CloudSEK_Admin", and "Guest".

EXPECTATION: Each thread prints its OWN user name, even though they all access
the same static variable 'UserSession.currentUser'.
================================================================================